SIGNOFF PERSON EXTRACTION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extract one object per signoff person. If multiple people signed, create separate objects for each.

FIELDS TO EXTRACT:

1. NAME
   Extract the full name of each person who signed the document.
   Source: Signature block, printed name below signature, or certified-by section.

2. DESIGNATION
   Extract the role/title of the signoff person (e.g., Director, Designated Member).
   If no designation is stated in the signature block, set "NA".

3. SPECIMEN
   If a handwritten or digital specimen signature is visually present in the document
   for that person, set "Snip provided".
   If no specimen is present, set "NA".

4. VERIFICATION CAPACITY
   Determine whether the signoff person's authority can be verified against a public
   registry based on the company's jurisdiction:
     • UK-registered company    → "Companies House UK"
     • India-registered company → If DIN is present in document, set "MCA India".
                                   Otherwise set "NA".
     • Other jurisdictions      → Set "NA" unless a specific public registry is
                                   identifiable from the document.

5. E-SIGNED OR WET INK SIGNED
     • DocuSign/eSign envelope ID or explicitly stated as electronically signed → "E-Signed"
     • Physical handwritten signature on scanned document with no e-sign indicators → "Wet Ink Signed"
     • If unclear → "NA"

OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:

{
  "Signoff_Persons": [
    {
      "Name": "John Smith",
      "Designation": "Director",
      "Specimen": "Snip provided",
      "Verification_Capacity": "Companies House UK",
      "E-Signed_or_Wet_Ink_Signed": "Wet Ink Signed"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Jane Doe",
      "Designation": "NA",
      "Specimen": "NA",
      "Verification_Capacity": "NA",
      "E-Signed_or_Wet_Ink_Signed": "E-Signed"
    }
  ]
}
